  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Cani Plouf occupies the Crique du Moulin, at the far end of Garonne beach in Le Pradet — a sheltered setting, away from the main swimming areas, designed entirely so dogs can enjoy it freely.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Outside this cove, Le Pradet's other beaches (such as Les Oursinières) only tolerate dogs on leash from 1 November to 31 March — so Cani Plouf remains the only reliable year-round option, including in the middle of summer.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if you're visiting in winter, you can also explore Les Oursinières beach with your dog on leash — a good complement to the dedicated cove.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Le Pradet's coastal path, which follows the shore between the coves, is a nice option for extending the outing on foot.</p>
